  "note": "Election of the fifteen councillors of the Enniskillen Borough Council, 1958; all were returned unopposed on nomination day, 6 May 1958 (Belfast Telegraph, 7 May 1958, p. 12), the six aldermen holding over. The Fermanagh Herald (17 May 1958, p. 3) and the Irish News (8 May 1958, p. 6) report ten Unionist and five Nationalist councillors, with Kerr succeeding Alderman T. Algeo and three Nationalist changes (Donnelly and Love for Nugent and Kelly, McCusker for McElroy). Labels are not printed in the list. Re-cited 7 Nov 2026: the earlier citation (Irish News, 8 May 1958, p. 3; News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6) does not carry these names. Ward breakdown as printed; the six aldermen held over. Returned unopposed."
